{
  "assessment": "The diff introduces four standalone modules (`charges.py`, `retry.py`, `sla.py`, `summary.py`) that implement billing, retry scheduling, SLA evaluation, and summary statistics respectively. None of them correctly account for the newly added `cancelled` status, leaving active decision paths to treat cancelled jobs as unfinished or eligible for further processing. As a result, cancelled work will incorrectly keep its SLA timer running, incur charges, land in an undocumented 'other' bucket, and remain candidates for automatic retries.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "It falls through to `return now`, causing the SLA calculation to use a moving target instead of the cancellation time. Cancelled jobs will show continuously worsening margins and false breaches.",
      "at": "`jobs/sla.py` (line 24 in `finished_at`)",
      "call": "python3 -c \"from jobs.sla import finished_at; from types import SimpleNamespace; j = SimpleNamespace(status='cancelled', ended_at=100); print(finished_at(j, now=500))\"",
      "defect": "`sla.py` does not treat cancelled jobs as finished",
      "expected": "The function should recognize `CANCELLED` as a terminal state and return `job.ended_at`, stopping the SLA clock."
    },
    {
      "actual": "`is_chargeable` returns `True` when `cpu_seconds > 0`, even if the job was cancelled by the system. Cancelled jobs will be billed incorrectly.",
      "at": "`jobs/charges.py` (line 35 in `is_chargeable`)",
      "call": "python3 -c \"from jobs.charges import is_chargeable; from types import SimpleNamespace; j = SimpleNamespace(status='cancelled', cpu_seconds=10); print(is_chargeable(j))\"",
      "defect": "`charges.py` charges cancelled jobs",
      "expected": "Billing should be voided for any job that was cancelled, matching the `FAILED` exclusion already present."
    },
    {
      "actual": "Cancelled jobs are silently grouped into `'other'`, making them invisible to dashboard queries and violating the spec that every status must have its own bucket.",
      "at": "`jobs/summary.py` (line 12-28 in `counts`)",
      "call": "python3 -c \"from jobs.summary import counts; from types import SimpleNamespace; j = SimpleNamespace(status='cancelled'); print(counts([j]))\"",
      "defect": "`summary.py` lacks a dedicated bucket for cancelled status",
      "expected": "A `'cancelled'` entry must be added to `BUCKETS` and handled in the `counts` logic so it is tracked separately."
    },
    {
      "actual": "`should_retry` only excludes `DONE`. A cancelled job with retries left passes through and gets requeued.",
      "at": "`jobs/retry.py` (line 21-35 in `should_retry`)",
      "call": "python3 -c \"from jobs.retry import should_retry; from types import SimpleNamespace; j = SimpleNamespace(status='cancelled', attempts=0, kind='render'); print(should_retry(j))\"",
      "defect": "`retry.py` allows retrying cancelled jobs",
      "expected": "The scheduler must immediately reject any job with a `CANCELLED` status, as work was explicitly halted."
    }
  ]
}
